Engine: the diplomacy audience reports its own screen ids, 57 and 58 (open fix 46).

STATUS: NOT APPLIED — written and proved by work order 185 (Part 9),
parked for Data (doc/briefs/185-parked-for-data.md). No engine patch may
be applied in that order.

PROOF (work order 185, 28 September 2026): in a scratch worktree of
orionlayer-local 4bf152e4 with its own build directory (never on
orionlayer-local itself, never the build play.py starts) this file applied
with `patch -p1 --dry-run` and `patch -p1`, no offset, no fuzz, and the
applied tree equals the scratch commit; the scratch engine was built in
full (Debug, ORION2RE_EXT=ON) — no error — dip_scrn_main.cpp compiles alone
with the build's own command, and a control, the same file with
`ScreenOverride` misspelt `ScreenOveride`, was refused by the compiler.
See the entry, doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md 46.

To apply, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_audience_screen.patch

then rebuild. It comes back off with `patch -R -p1` and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    The diplomacy audience has no screen id: DIP_SCRN::Diplomacy_Screen_
    (the player's, from the Races screen) and Npc_Diplomacy_Screen_ (the
    AI's — at turn start from report.cpp, on a sneak attack from
    combfind.cpp) run under their caller's id, 6, 0 or 12, so a client
    cannot tell the audience is up. The patch makes each report a
    synthetic id through ext::ScreenOverride (open fix 24's pattern: what
    is SENT, nothing the game reads): 57 the player's, 58 the AI's. A
    marker, `OrionLayer, open fix 46.`, on one line at every changed place.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.h b/src/ext/ext_api.h
index c228885f..700571e3 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.h
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.h
@@ -44,6 +44,12 @@ struct ScreenOverride {
     ~ScreenOverride();
 };
 
+/// OrionLayer, open fix 46. The diplomacy audience has no screen id and runs under its
+/// caller's (6 the Races screen, 0 a turn-start report, 12 a sneak attack
+/// in turn processing): it reports 57 when the player opened it
+/// (DIP_SCRN::Diplomacy_Screen_) and 58 when an AI asked for it
+/// (DIP_SCRN::Npc_Diplomacy_Screen_), so a client can tell it is up.
+
 /// The field id of the input Get_Input_() is returning THIS CALL when it
 /// came from a client's ACTIVATE_FIELD, and 0 when it came from the mouse.
 ///
diff --git a/src/game/dip_scrn_main.cpp b/src/game/dip_scrn_main.cpp
index a534a3b4..e3025c66 100644
--- a/src/game/dip_scrn_main.cpp
+++ b/src/game/dip_scrn_main.cpp
@@ -1,4 +1,7 @@
 #include "pch.h"
+#ifdef ORION2RE_EXT
+#include "ext/ext_api.h"  // OrionLayer, open fix 46. ScreenOverride for the two audiences.
+#endif
 
 namespace DIP_SCRN {
     /**
@@ -1255,6 +1258,10 @@ namespace DIP_SCRN {
     }
 
     void __cdecl Diplomacy_Screen_(int player_idx) {
+#ifdef ORION2RE_EXT
+        // OrionLayer, open fix 46. The player's audience reports a synthetic 57 (ext_api.h); the game still reads its caller's screen.
+        const ext::ScreenOverride ext_screen_guard(57);
+#endif
         _diplomacy_current_music = -1;
         _synch_up_established_flag = 0;
 
@@ -1352,6 +1359,10 @@ namespace DIP_SCRN {
         if (MOX::_player[player_idx].eliminated == 1) {
             return;
         }
+#ifdef ORION2RE_EXT
+        // OrionLayer, open fix 46. An audience the AI asked for (turn start, report.cpp; a sneak attack, combfind.cpp) reports a synthetic 58 (ext_api.h).
+        const ext::ScreenOverride ext_screen_guard(58);
+#endif
 
         fields::Deactivate_Help_List_();
         fields::Enable_Draw_All_Fields_();
